bitscan-agent (0.2.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Release 0.2.0 of the Bitscan agent, with manager 0.2.0: compliance
    scans, their results and retention.
  * bitscan-runner runs the checks of compliance jobs in its sandbox as
    the unprivileged bitscan-runner user and returns their output
    redacted on the host. bitscan-agent keeps the results in its on-disk
    spool until the manager has answered them. Inventory runs as before.
  * Manager 0.2.0 runs scans of one compliance profile on a host, a tag
    or the whole fleet, by hand or on a schedule. It shows each host's
    results and score, exports them as CSV and re-evaluates them. Its
    retention job deletes old scans, inventory and other data.
  * Known limit: the manager importer's command check (BIT102) is a
    safety net, and the runner sandbox is the real control. In this
    release the importer does not check command strings passed to su,
    runuser or flock with -c, trap, brace expansion in bash -c scripts,
    commands behind the wrappers time, nsenter, unshare, flock, setpriv,
    taskset, chrt, runuser and su, long options given as abbreviations
    to the wrappers it does check (for example sudo --us), the output
    files that time -o or --output and flock open, or a command word
    that is not literal, such as one taken from a variable.
  * The sample policies in bits/samples/ are not part of this package or
    the manager release. Their CIS control numbers are not yet confirmed
    against the CIS benchmark.
  * Supported with manager 0.2.0 and manager 0.1.0. Manager 0.1.0 has no
    scans, so it sends this agent no compliance job.
  * Upgrades 0.1.0-1 and the 0.2.0~pre1-1 and 0.2.0~pre2-1 pre-releases
    in place and keeps their configuration, agent token and agent id.

 -- Bitdeer-Security <kaiquan.koh@bitdeer.com>  Wed, 11 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000

bitscan-agent (0.2.0~pre2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Pre-release: results and end to end. Not a supported release.
  * Built for the manager's scan results views and the nightly end-to-end
    run. Enrolment, heartbeat, inventory and the job protocol are as in
    0.2.0~pre1-1.
  * bitscan-runner.service makes /dev/shm read-only and lists /tmp and
    /var/tmp in NoExecPaths=, so a check can neither leave files in the
    host's shared memory nor run a file it wrote to its private /tmp.
  * bitscan-runner is ready for the next job as soon as the previous one
    and its cleanup have ended, and takes no job after a failed cleanup.
  * Upgrades 0.1.0-1 and 0.2.0~pre1-1 in place and keeps their
    configuration, agent token and agent id.

 -- Bitdeer-Security <kaiquan.koh@bitdeer.com>  Sun, 08 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000

bitscan-agent (0.2.0~pre1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Pre-release: compliance runner. Not a supported release.
  * bitscan-runner runs the checks of compliance jobs in its sandbox and
    returns redacted output. It refuses to start without the unified
    cgroup v2 hierarchy, and the agent then reports each check as
    runner_unavailable.
  * bitscan-agent hands compliance jobs to the runner and keeps their
    results in an on-disk spool (spool_max_mb) until the manager has
    answered them. Inventory runs as before.
  * bitscan-capread answers nft_ruleset and audit_rules. It stays disabled
    until an administrator enables bitscan-capread.socket on the host.
  * Upgrades 0.1.0-1 in place and keeps its configuration, agent token
    and agent id.

 -- Bitdeer-Security <kaiquan.koh@bitdeer.com>  Fri, 30 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000

bitscan-agent (0.1.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * First supported release of the Bitscan agent: enrolment, heartbeat,
    job pull and mandatory inventory. Compliance scans are not in 0.1.0:
    the runner and the capread helper stay idle, and every check of a
    compliance job is reported as runner_unavailable.
  * Upgrades the 0.1.0~pre1-1 pre-release in place and keeps its
    configuration, agent token and agent id.

